  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Savanti Romero's last ability counts all counters on Savanti Romero, not just +1/+1 counters.",
      "oracle_id": "6074632b-4520-4ae8-bcdc-26b1eff71af9",
      "published_at": "2026-01-27",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The value of X is calculated only once, as Savanti Romero's last ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "6074632b-4520-4ae8-bcdc-26b1eff71af9",
      "published_at": "2026-01-27",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Assemble the Legion isn't on the battlefield when its ability resolves, use the number of muster counters it had when it was last on the battlefield to determine how many Soldier tokens to create.",
      "oracle_id": "6f81bef3-6ca0-4cf4-aa99-7b2813eeef04",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Insight Engine leaves the battlefield before its ability resolves, it won\u2019t have a charge counter put on it when the ability resolves. Use the number of charge counters on it as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how many cards to draw.",
      "oracle_id": "83409a22-10de-4d51-90a3-e0579ca8cbea",
      "published_at": "2025-07-25",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.",
      "oracle_id": "a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6",
      "published_at": "2023-09-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells that were cast before a permanent with flurry count. If that permanent was the first spell you cast that turn, the next spell you cast that turn is your second spell.",
      "oracle_id": "ae61b2ef-2e60-499a-8708-e37b9bd5620e",
      "published_at": "2025-04-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If Krenko leaves the battlefield after its ability has triggered but before it resolves, you don't put a +1/+1 counter on it, but you do use its power as it last existed before it left the battlefield to determine how many Goblin tokens to create.",
      "oracle_id": "e8065e1d-e937-4b56-8011-78f0d07328a0",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The tokens created by Krenko's triggered ability aren't attacking. Because all attackers are chosen at once, a token created this way can't attack, even if it gains haste.",
      "oracle_id": "e8065e1d-e937-4b56-8011-78f0d07328a0",
      "published_at": "2019-05-03",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
